{"id":"s4.5.3","slug":"repeating-decimals-in-other-bases-to-base-10","title":"Repeating Decimals in Other Bases - Convert to Base 10","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">To convert a repeating decimal in another base to a base-10 fraction, you can use the infinite geometric series formula or apply the same logic as base-10 repeating decimals, but with the new base.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For $.xyxy..._b$, the base-10 fraction is $\\frac{(xy)_b}{b^2-1}$, where $(xy)_b$ is first converted to base 10.</p><p>For $.xyyy..._b$, the fraction is $\\frac{(xy)_b - x}{b(b-1)}$.</p><p>Example: $.3535..._8$. The numerator is $35_8 = 3 \\times 8 + 5 = 29_{10}$. The denominator is $8^2-1=63$. The fraction is $\\frac{29}{63}$.</p>","summary":"To convert a repeating decimal in another base to a base-10 fraction, you can use the infinite geometric series formula or apply the same logic as bas","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem converting a repeating decimal in a base other than 10 to a base-10 fraction.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Change $0.111..._3$ to a base-10 fraction.","answer":"1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","repeating-decimals","conversions"]},{"id":2,"text":"Change $0.222..._4$ to a base-10 fraction.","answer":"2/3","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","repeating-decimals","conversions"]},{"id":3,"text":"Change $0.333..._5$ to a base-10 fraction.","answer":"3/4","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","repeating-decimals","conversions"]},{"id":4,"text":"Change $0.444..._6$ to a base-10 fraction.","answer":"4/5","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","repeating-decimals","conversions"]},{"id":5,"text":"Change $0.555..._7$ to a base-10 fraction.","answer":"5/6","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","repeating-decimals","conversions"]},{"id":6,"text":"Change $0.666..._8$ to a base-10 fraction.","answer":"6/7","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","repeating-decimals","conversions"]},{"id":7,"text":"Change $0.777..._9$ to a base-10 fracti